---
import Layout from '~/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import Hero from '~/components/widgets/Hero.astro';
import Content from '~/components/widgets/Content.astro';
import Features3 from '~/components/widgets/Features3.astro';

const metadata = {
  title: 'Your First API Call — A Developer Onboarding Simulation',
};
---

<Layout metadata={metadata}>
  <Hero tagline="Instructional Design · Articulate Storyline 360 · Software Simulation · JavaScript Integration">
    <Fragment slot="title">
      Your First API Call —<br />
      <span class="text-accent dark:text-white">A Developer Onboarding Simulation</span>
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="subtitle">
      A technical instructional design portfolio piece targeting developer audiences — needs analysis, learning
      objectives, content map, and a Storyline 360 software simulation with custom JavaScript-generated integration
      audit reporting.
    </Fragment>
  </Hero>

  <!-- Context -->
  <Content tagline="The Problem" title="Most developers learn API integration the hard way — in production" isReversed>
    <Fragment slot="image">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-center h-full py-12">
        <div class="text-center">
          <p class="text-7xl font-bold font-heading text-accent leading-none">68%</p>
          <p class="text-xl text-muted mt-3">of API security incidents involve improper credential handling</p>
          <div class="mt-8 space-y-2 text-sm text-muted">
            <p class="font-semibold text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
              Salt Security State of API Security Report 2024
            </p>
            <p>Average cost of an API breach: $6.1M</p>
            <p>Articulate Storyline 360 · JavaScript</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="content">
      <p class="mb-4">
        New developers joining technical teams spend their first weeks reading API documentation — passively absorbing
        endpoint references, authentication schemas, and rate limit tables. No one practices the actual decisions. The
        first time they encounter a 401 Unauthorized or a 429 Too Many Requests, it's in production, with real
        consequences.
      </p>
      <p class="mb-4">
        The cost of poor API hygiene compounds fast. An API key exposed in a URL query parameter shows up in server
        logs, browser history, and HTTP referrer headers. Hard-coded credentials committed to a shared repository become
        a breach waiting for a bad actor. Tight retry loops on rate-limited endpoints escalate to IP bans that take down
        entire integration pipelines.
      </p>
      <p>
        This module places developers inside a realistic first-day integration scenario — three decisions, real
        technical consequences, and a JavaScript-generated audit report tied to their exact choices.
      </p>
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="bg">
      <div class="absolute inset-0 section-pattern-b"></div>
    </Fragment>
  </Content>

  <!-- Design Process -->
  <Features3
    tagline="Design Process"
    title="From performance gap to developer simulation"
    subtitle="Following the full instructional design process — analysis, objectives, content map, build, and evaluation planning."
    columns={3}
    items={[
      {
        title: 'Needs Analysis',
        description:
          'Identified the root cause before writing a single objective. Developer onboarding failures are not a documentation problem — they are a decision-making gap. New engineers know what an API key is; they do not know which authentication pattern to use or why it matters. Simulation-based practice was the right intervention.',
        icon: 'tabler:search',
      },
      {
        title: 'Learning Objectives',
        description:
          "Four objectives written to Bloom's Taxonomy — progressing from selecting a secure authentication method (Application) through implementing error handling (Application) to evaluating a rate-limit response strategy (Analysis) and interpreting a personalized integration audit (Evaluation).",
        icon: 'tabler:target',
      },
      {
        title: 'Content Map',
        description:
          'A full 14-slide content map documented before building — mapping each decision point, branching path, variable trigger, consequence screen, and debrief to specific learning objectives and real-world developer failure modes sourced from the Salt Security and OWASP API Security Top 10.',
        icon: 'tabler:layout-board',
      },
      {
        title: 'Branching Architecture',
        description:
          'Three decision points track distinct API security and reliability categories: credential handling (authentication method), resilience (error handling), and rate limit strategy. Wrong answers produce technical consequence screens grounded in real failure data — not grade penalties.',
        icon: 'tabler:git-branch',
      },
      {
        title: 'JavaScript Integration',
        description:
          "Four Storyline variables — authMethod, errorHandling, rateLimitStrategy, and integrationScore — are read by a custom JavaScript trigger at the end of the module. The trigger generates a personalized API Integration Audit Report based on the developer's exact decision path.",
        icon: 'tabler:code',
      },
      {
        title: 'Source Content Synthesis',
        description:
          'Consequence screens are grounded in real industry data synthesized via NotebookLM — Salt Security breach cost figures, OWASP API Security Top 10 findings, and AWS rate-limiting best practices. The 68% credential mishandling figure and $6.1M average breach cost are sourced, not invented.',
        icon: 'tabler:database',
      },
    ]}
  />

  <!-- Module Embed -->
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 md:px-8 py-12 md:py-16">
    <div class="text-center mb-10">
      <p class="text-base text-secondary dark:text-blue-200 font-bold tracking-wide uppercase mb-2">Storyline Module</p>
      <h2 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tighter font-heading">Take the Simulation</h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-muted mt-4">
        A Storyline 360 developer simulation — three API integration decisions, real technical consequences, and a
        JavaScript-generated audit report personalized to your exact decision path.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div
      class="relative w-full rounded-lg shadow-lg overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700"
      style="padding-top: 62.5%;"
    >
      <iframe
        class="absolute inset-0 w-full h-full"
        src="/rest-api-simulation-content/story.html"
        title="Your First API Call — Developer Onboarding Simulation"
        frameborder="0"
        allowfullscreen></iframe>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Learning Objectives -->
  <Content tagline="Learning Design" title="Objectives written to Bloom's Taxonomy" isReversed>
    <Fragment slot="image">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-center h-full py-12 px-6">
        <div class="w-full max-w-xs space-y-3">
          {
            [
              {
                label: 'Select a secure API authentication method',
                detail: 'Application — prevent credential exposure and unauthorized access',
                color: 'blue',
              },
              {
                label: 'Implement error handling for API responses',
                detail: 'Application — prevent silent failures and production crashes',
                color: 'green',
              },
              {
                label: 'Evaluate a rate-limit response strategy',
                detail: 'Analysis — choose exponential backoff over tight retry loops',
                color: 'purple',
              },
              {
                label: 'Interpret an API integration audit report',
                detail: 'Evaluation — assess decision quality and production risk',
                color: 'orange',
              },
            ].map(({ label, detail, color }) => (
              <div
                class={`flex items-start gap-3 p-2.5 rounded-lg border ${color === 'blue' ? 'border-blue-200 dark:border-blue-800 bg-blue-50 dark:bg-blue-900/20' : color === 'green' ? 'border-green-200 dark:border-green-800 bg-green-50 dark:bg-green-900/20' : color === 'purple' ? 'border-purple-200 dark:border-purple-800 bg-purple-50 dark:bg-purple-900/20' : 'border-orange-200 dark:border-orange-800 bg-orange-50 dark:bg-orange-900/20'}`}
              >
                <div>
                  <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200">{label}</p>
                  <p class="text-xs text-muted mt-0.5">{detail}</p>
                </div>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </div>
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="content">
      <p class="mb-4">
        The four learning objectives follow a deliberate Bloom's Taxonomy progression — two at Application (selecting,
        implementing), one at Analysis (evaluating a strategy), and one at Evaluation (interpreting the audit output).
        All four tie directly to measurable developer performance on the first day of API integration work.
      </p>
      <p class="mb-4">
        The most common failure mode for new developers is not ignorance of REST conventions — they know what GET and
        POST mean. The gap is judgment: which authentication pattern is actually secure, what happens when you ignore a
        500 error, and why retrying 200 times in two seconds is worse than waiting. Decisions 1 through 3 are designed
        to build exactly that judgment.
      </p>
      <p>
        The JavaScript audit report at the end of the module connects all three decisions to a production-risk rating —
        making the consequence of each choice concrete before the developer faces it in a real codebase.
      </p>
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="bg">
      <div class="absolute inset-0 section-pattern"></div>
    </Fragment>
  </Content>

  <!-- Branching Diagram -->
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 md:px-8 py-12 md:py-16">
    <div class="text-center mb-10">
      <p class="text-base text-secondary dark:text-blue-200 font-bold tracking-wide uppercase mb-2">
        Branching Architecture
      </p>
      <h2 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tighter font-heading">Three Decisions. Eight Paths.</h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-muted mt-4 max-w-2xl mx-auto">
        Every choice triggers a variable update and routes to a distinct consequence or confirmation screen before
        converging at the JavaScript-generated API integration audit report.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-lg border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 bg-white dark:bg-gray-900 p-4 overflow-x-auto">
      <svg
        viewBox="0 0 820 620"
        xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
        role="img"
        style="width:100%;max-width:820px;display:block;margin:0 auto;"
        font-family="Arial, sans-serif"
      >
        <title>REST API Developer Simulation Branching Diagram</title>
        <desc
          >A flowchart showing three API integration decision points with branching consequence and correct paths
          leading to a JavaScript-generated audit report.</desc
        >
        <defs>
          <marker id="arrow" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" refX="6" refY="3" orient="auto"
            ><path d="M0,0 L0,6 L8,3 z" fill="#6b7280"></path></marker
          >
          <marker id="arrow-red" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" refX="6" refY="3" orient="auto"
            ><path d="M0,0 L0,6 L8,3 z" fill="#dc2626"></path></marker
          >
          <marker id="arrow-green" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" refX="6" refY="3" orient="auto"
            ><path d="M0,0 L0,6 L8,3 z" fill="#16a34a"></path></marker
          >
          <marker id="arrow-amber" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" refX="6" refY="3" orient="auto"
            ><path d="M0,0 L0,6 L8,3 z" fill="#d97706"></path></marker
          >
        </defs>
        <!-- START -->
        <rect x="310" y="10" width="200" height="44" rx="8" fill="#0f766e"></rect>
        <text x="410" y="28" text-anchor="middle" fill="white" font-size="11" font-weight="bold">SLIDE 1–2</text>
        <text x="410" y="44" text-anchor="middle" fill="white" font-size="11">Hook + Meet Alex Chen</text>
        <line x1="410" y1="54" x2="410" y2="78" stroke="#6b7280" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#arrow)"></line>
        <!-- DECISION 1 -->
        <rect x="285" y="80" width="250" height="48" rx="8" fill="#134e4a"></rect>
        <text x="410" y="99" text-anchor="middle" fill="white" font-size="11" font-weight="bold"
          >DECISION 1 — SLIDE 3</text
        >
        <text x="410" y="116" text-anchor="middle" fill="#99f6e4" font-size="10">Authentication Method</text>
        <line x1="285" y1="104" x2="130" y2="104" stroke="#dc2626" stroke-width="1.5"></line>
        <line x1="130" y1="104" x2="130" y2="178" stroke="#dc2626" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#arrow-red)"
        ></line>
        <text x="200" y="98" text-anchor="middle" fill="#dc2626" font-size="9">Choice A</text>
        <line x1="410" y1="128" x2="410" y2="178" stroke="#d97706" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#arrow-amber)"
        ></line>
        <text x="425" y="160" fill="#d97706" font-size="9">Choice B</text>
        <line x1="535" y1="104" x2="680" y2="104" stroke="#16a34a" stroke-width="1.5"></line>
        <line x1="680" y1="104" x2="680" y2="178" stroke="#16a34a" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#arrow-green)"
        ></line>
        <text x="600" y="98" text-anchor="middle" fill="#16a34a" font-size="9">Choice C ✓</text>
        <!-- D1 Consequences -->
        <rect x="50" y="180" width="160" height="52" rx="6" fill="#fef2f2" stroke="#dc2626" stroke-width="1.5"></rect>
        <text x="130" y="198" text-anchor="middle" fill="#dc2626" font-size="10" font-weight="bold">KEY IN URL</text>
        <text x="130" y="212" text-anchor="middle" fill="#7f1d1d" font-size="9">Exposed in logs · $6.1M risk</text>
        <text x="130" y="224" text-anchor="middle" fill="#9ca3af" font-size="9">Slide 4 → Try Again</text>
        <path
          d="M50,206 C20,206 20,104 285,104"
          stroke="#dc2626"
          stroke-width="1"
          stroke-dasharray="4,3"
          fill="none"
          marker-end="url(#arrow-red)"></path>
        <rect x="330" y="180" width="160" height="52" rx="6" fill="#fffbeb" stroke="#d97706" stroke-width="1.5"></rect>
        <text x="410" y="198" text-anchor="middle" fill="#d97706" font-size="10" font-weight="bold">KEY HARD-CODED</text
        >
        <text x="410" y="212" text-anchor="middle" fill="#78350f" font-size="9">integrationScore +20</text>
        <text x="410" y="224" text-anchor="middle" fill="#9ca3af" font-size="9">Slide 5 → continues</text>
        <rect x="600" y="180" width="160" height="52" rx="6" fill="#f0fdf4" stroke="#16a34a" stroke-width="1.5"></rect>
        <text x="680" y="198" text-anchor="middle" fill="#16a34a" font-size="10" font-weight="bold"
          >SECURE HEADER ✓</text
        >
        <text x="680" y="212" text-anchor="middle" fill="#14532d" font-size="9">Env variable · zero exposure</text>
        <text x="680" y="224" text-anchor="middle" fill="#9ca3af" font-size="9">Slide 6 → continues</text>
        <!-- D1 → D2 -->
        <line x1="410" y1="232" x2="410" y2="268" stroke="#d97706" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#arrow-amber)"
        ></line>
        <line x1="680" y1="232" x2="680" y2="260" stroke="#16a34a" stroke-width="1.5"></line>
        <line x1="680" y1="260" x2="535" y2="268" stroke="#16a34a" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#arrow-green)"
        ></line>
        <!-- DECISION 2 -->
        <rect x="285" y="270" width="250" height="48" rx="8" fill="#134e4a"></rect>
        <text x="410" y="289" text-anchor="middle" fill="white" font-size="11" font-weight="bold"
          >DECISION 2 — SLIDE 7</text
        >
        <text x="410" y="306" text-anchor="middle" fill="#99f6e4" font-size="10">Error Handling Strategy</text>
        <line x1="285" y1="294" x2="130" y2="294" stroke="#dc2626" stroke-width="1.5"></line>
        <line x1="130" y1="294" x2="130" y2="368" stroke="#dc2626" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#arrow-red)"
        ></line>
        <text x="200" y="288" text-anchor="middle" fill="#dc2626" font-size="9">Choice A</text>
        <line x1="535" y1="294" x2="680" y2="294" stroke="#16a34a" stroke-width="1.5"></line>
        <line x1="680" y1="294" x2="680" y2="368" stroke="#16a34a" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#arrow-green)"
        ></line>
        <text x="600" y="288" text-anchor="middle" fill="#16a34a" font-size="9">Choice B ✓</text>
        <line x1="410" y1="318" x2="410" y2="368" stroke="#d97706" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#arrow-amber)"
        ></line>
        <text x="425" y="350" fill="#d97706" font-size="9">Choice C</text>
        <!-- D2 Consequences -->
        <rect x="50" y="370" width="160" height="52" rx="6" fill="#fef2f2" stroke="#dc2626" stroke-width="1.5"></rect>
        <text x="130" y="388" text-anchor="middle" fill="#dc2626" font-size="10" font-weight="bold">PROD CRASH</text>
        <text x="130" y="402" text-anchor="middle" fill="#7f1d1d" font-size="9">Unhandled 500 · pipeline down</text>
        <text x="130" y="414" text-anchor="middle" fill="#9ca3af" font-size="9">Slide 8 → Try Again</text>
        <path
          d="M50,396 C20,396 20,294 285,294"
          stroke="#dc2626"
          stroke-width="1"
          stroke-dasharray="4,3"
          fill="none"
          marker-end="url(#arrow-red)"></path>
        <rect x="330" y="370" width="160" height="52" rx="6" fill="#fffbeb" stroke="#d97706" stroke-width="1.5"></rect>
        <text x="410" y="388" text-anchor="middle" fill="#d97706" font-size="10" font-weight="bold">SILENT FAILURE</text
        >
        <text x="410" y="402" text-anchor="middle" fill="#78350f" font-size="9">integrationScore +15</text>
        <text x="410" y="414" text-anchor="middle" fill="#9ca3af" font-size="9">Slide 10 → continues</text>
        <rect x="600" y="370" width="160" height="52" rx="6" fill="#f0fdf4" stroke="#16a34a" stroke-width="1.5"></rect>
        <text x="680" y="388" text-anchor="middle" fill="#16a34a" font-size="10" font-weight="bold">RESILIENT ✓</text>
        <text x="680" y="402" text-anchor="middle" fill="#14532d" font-size="9">Try/catch · status codes checked</text>
        <text x="680" y="414" text-anchor="middle" fill="#9ca3af" font-size="9">Slide 9 → continues</text>
        <!-- D2 → D3 -->
        <line x1="410" y1="422" x2="410" y2="458" stroke="#d97706" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#arrow-amber)"
        ></line>
        <line x1="680" y1="422" x2="680" y2="450" stroke="#16a34a" stroke-width="1.5"></line>
        <line x1="680" y1="450" x2="535" y2="458" stroke="#16a34a" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#arrow-green)"
        ></line>
        <!-- DECISION 3 -->
        <rect x="285" y="460" width="250" height="48" rx="8" fill="#134e4a"></rect>
        <text x="410" y="479" text-anchor="middle" fill="white" font-size="11" font-weight="bold"
          >DECISION 3 — SLIDE 11</text
        >
        <text x="410" y="496" text-anchor="middle" fill="#99f6e4" font-size="10">Rate Limit Response</text>
        <line x1="535" y1="484" x2="620" y2="484" stroke="#16a34a" stroke-width="1.5"></line>
        <line x1="620" y1="484" x2="620" y2="548" stroke="#16a34a" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#arrow-green)"
        ></line>
        <text x="572" y="478" text-anchor="middle" fill="#16a34a" font-size="9">Choice A ✓</text>
        <line x1="285" y1="484" x2="200" y2="484" stroke="#dc2626" stroke-width="1.5"></line>
        <line x1="200" y1="484" x2="200" y2="548" stroke="#dc2626" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#arrow-red)"
        ></line>
        <text x="238" y="478" text-anchor="middle" fill="#dc2626" font-size="9">Choice B</text>
        <!-- D3 Consequences -->
        <rect x="110" y="550" width="180" height="44" rx="6" fill="#fef2f2" stroke="#dc2626" stroke-width="1.5"></rect>
        <text x="200" y="568" text-anchor="middle" fill="#dc2626" font-size="10" font-weight="bold">IP BANNED</text>
        <text x="200" y="582" text-anchor="middle" fill="#7f1d1d" font-size="9">Slide 13 · integrationScore +25</text>
        <rect x="530" y="550" width="180" height="44" rx="6" fill="#f0fdf4" stroke="#16a34a" stroke-width="1.5"></rect>
        <text x="620" y="568" text-anchor="middle" fill="#16a34a" font-size="10" font-weight="bold"
          >BACKOFF IMPL. ✓</text
        >
        <text x="620" y="582" text-anchor="middle" fill="#14532d" font-size="9">Slide 12 · pipeline stable</text>
        <!-- Both → Audit -->
        <line x1="200" y1="594" x2="200" y2="610" stroke="#6b7280" stroke-width="1.5"></line>
        <line x1="200" y1="610" x2="380" y2="610" stroke="#6b7280" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#arrow)"></line>
        <line x1="620" y1="594" x2="620" y2="610" stroke="#6b7280" stroke-width="1.5"></line>
        <line x1="620" y1="610" x2="440" y2="610" stroke="#6b7280" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#arrow)"></line>
        <!-- AUDIT REPORT -->
        <rect x="310" y="590" width="200" height="26" rx="6" fill="#0f766e"></rect>
        <text x="410" y="608" text-anchor="middle" fill="white" font-size="11" font-weight="bold"
          >AUDIT REPORT — SLIDE 14</text
        >
        <!-- LEGEND -->
        <rect x="10" y="10" width="130" height="80" rx="6" fill="none" stroke="#e5e7eb" stroke-width="1"></rect>
        <text x="20" y="26" fill="#6b7280" font-size="9" font-weight="bold">LEGEND</text>
        <rect x="20" y="34" width="10" height="10" rx="2" fill="#dc2626"></rect>
        <text x="36" y="43" fill="#374151" font-size="9">Consequence</text>
        <rect x="20" y="50" width="10" height="10" rx="2" fill="#d97706"></rect>
        <text x="36" y="59" fill="#374151" font-size="9">Warning / Risk</text>
        <rect x="20" y="66" width="10" height="10" rx="2" fill="#16a34a"></rect>
        <text x="36" y="75" fill="#374151" font-size="9">Correct Path</text>
        <line x1="20" y1="84" x2="30" y2="84" stroke="#dc2626" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="3,2"></line>
        <text x="36" y="88" fill="#374151" font-size="9">Try Again</text>
      </svg>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Slide Outline -->
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 md:px-8 py-12 md:py-16">
    <div class="text-center mb-10">
      <p class="text-base text-secondary dark:text-blue-200 font-bold tracking-wide uppercase mb-2">
        Instructional Arc
      </p>
      <h2 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tighter font-heading">
        14 Slides. 3 Decisions. 1 Audit Report.
      </h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-muted mt-4 max-w-2xl mx-auto">
        Each slide maps to a deliberate phase — Hook, Setup, Decision, Consequence, or Debrief — moving the developer
        from framing to action to personalized reflection.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 shadow-sm">
      <table class="w-full text-sm text-left">
        <thead>
          <tr class="bg-teal-900 text-white">
            <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold w-10">#</th>
            <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold w-28">Phase</th>
            <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold w-44">Slide Title</th>
            <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Content Summary</th>
            <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold w-48">Interaction</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="divide-y divide-gray-200 dark:divide-gray-700">
          {
            [
              {
                num: '1',
                phase: 'Hook',
                phaseColor: 'text-pink-600 dark:text-pink-400',
                title: 'Your First API Call',
                content:
                  "Day 5. The payment processing API is live. The tech lead just dropped the docs in Slack. It's your job to integrate it.",
                interaction: 'Title card, Begin button',
              },
              {
                num: '2',
                phase: 'Setup',
                phaseColor: 'text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400',
                title: 'Meet Alex Chen',
                content:
                  'Junior Backend Developer, first week on the FinTech team. Task: integrate the internal payment API into the checkout flow. API key just landed in email.',
                interaction: 'Character card with role context',
              },
              {
                num: '3',
                phase: 'Decision',
                phaseColor: 'text-green-600 dark:text-green-400',
                title: 'Decision 1: Authentication',
                content:
